=begin pod

<p align="center"><img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/podlite/podlite-desktop/v0.9.0/release-notes/assets/v0.9.0/hero-v0.9.0.png" alt="Podlite Desktop 0.9.0" width="900"></p>

=head3 Markdown, first class

Open a C<.md> file and the editor highlights it as Markdown, the preview renders
it as Markdown, and a double-click or a drop opens it straight away. Podlite
takes Markdown in, so this is the same editor, not a second mode.

<p align="center"><img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/podlite/podlite-desktop/v0.9.0/doc/markdown-highlighting.png" alt="A Markdown file: highlighted source on the left, rendered preview on the right" width="900"></p>

=head3 The document, read as a tree

Highlighting no longer works line by line. Every markup code gets its colour, a
section name reads apart from a block name you brought in yourself, the settings
inside a markdown fence are coloured the same way in a C<.podlite> file and in a
C<.md> one, and C«G<>» content shows as a covered strip that opens under the caret.

<p align="center"><img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/podlite/podlite-desktop/v0.9.0/doc/podlite-highlighting.png" alt="A Podlite document: every markup code coloured, preview on the right" width="900"></p>

=include file:../CHANGELOG.podlite | pod[:released-in<0.9.0>]

=end pod
